/w) values of the platinum(IV) complexes 1 and 7 were tested by the shake flask method. Briefly, n-octanol used in the experiment was presaturated with ultrapure water containing 0.9% NaCl (w/v) overnight. (56) An n-octanol solution of platinum(IV) complex (1 mM) was added to an equal volume of ultrapure water with 0.9% NaCl (w/v), and the mixture was shaking for 30 min vigorously. After that, the mixture was centrifuged at 2000 rpm for 15 min to achieve phase separation. The amount of the complex in n-octanol and water phases was determined by HPLC. The results were obtained based on three parallel experiments. The Log Po/w values of CDDP and OLP were obtained from the literature. (45)"}]}